{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Issues in the Workplace", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Going Green", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "extended period", "type": "name"}, {"content": "long or longer than the usual a \u200blength of \u200btime", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Personal printers in offices must be turned off when not in use for extended periods as well. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about solutions to environmental problems. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "standby mode ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a particular way in which a machine is in low-power timeout stage", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Even in standby mode they are consuming energy and costing us money!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "automatically", "type": "name"}, {"content": "doing something \u200bindependently, without \u200bhuman \u200bcontrol", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I'll be looking into the installation of software that automatically turns the machine off at a certain time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "preset time ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "\u200bpreparing a \u200bmachine so it will \u200boperate or \u200bstop \u200bat a specified time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It needs to automatically turn on at a preset time in the morning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to power up ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bturn on or \u200bprepare so that it is \u200bready for use or \u200baction", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We needn't have it powered up all night. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "energy efficient ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "using little electricity ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It doesn't look like there are many energy efficient features. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "exceptionally", "type": "name"}, {"content": " much greater than usual in quantity ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If it takes an exceptionally long time to warm up then there's no use. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "If-Clauses Used in Polite Requests", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> in if-clauses for polite requests.</br> These are especially useful in a workplace setting.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at the following example: </br></br> <span class=\"italic\">If you <span class=\"strong\">would </span>be kind enough to lend me a hand, we could finish this very quickly.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structuring a request in this way is a very polite way to address your colleagues. It is not common to hear this in everyday conversation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here is another example:  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">If you <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't</span> mind checking this for me ... </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You do not need to finish the sentence - it is polite as it stands.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you would let me know what you're looking for, I would be more than happy to help you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you wouldn't mind filling in this survey before you go, you can leave it at my desk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would appreciate it if you would tell me whether the standby is set properly on this machine. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wanted to know if you would walk me through this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you wouldn't mind answering some of my questions. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Expressing Necessity", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the modals <span class=\"strong\">must</span>, <span class=\"strong\">need </span> and their negatives <span class=\"strong\">mustn't</span> and <span class=\"strong\">needn't</span> to talk about what is necessary and not necessary.<br> <br> You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> or <span class=\"strong\">need </span> when something is necessary to be done. <br>  Example: <span class=\"italic\"><br>There is not enough time. You <span class=\"strong\"> must</span> hurry up / you <span class=\"strong\">need </span> to hurry up. </span> <br> <br> You use <span class=\"strong\">mustn't</span> when something is prohibited. <br> Example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> You <span class=\"strong\">mustn't</span> play here. This is a church. </span> <br> <br> You use <span class=\"strong\">needn't</span> when there is no necessity to do something. <br> Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\"> You <span class=\"strong\">needn't</span> close the doors after leaving. </span> (You don't have to close the doors, but if you do it's OK.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We need to switch printers off at the end of the workday if possible. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We needn't have it powered up all night. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Personal printers in offices must be turned off when not in use.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You musn't be touching that. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le15ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss environmental issues with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a letter to a city official.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give my point of view.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I propose solutions using modals for necessity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my letter to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, discuss environmental problems in your area.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one problem.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss what can be done to solve this problem.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a letter to a city official informing them of your view.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Propose solutions to this problem. Use modals to express necessity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the correct structure of a letter, including a salutation and a final closing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your letter to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about solving problems. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can describe environmental problems. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express necessity, duty, and advice. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Can you think of any major environmental problems in your city? What about in your country? 